From 0021469ff46b0bf44f066f043b82231ce73032fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Bulashev <d.bulashev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:39:50 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] pathprobe: move the kept annotation out of label

The probe0 and probe2 survivor snapshots wrote "  kept: startup" and
"  kept: order?" into the label field, which otherwise names a proposed
or hypothetical path.  JSON derives origin from label, so a real path
kept for its startup cost or its order came out as "origin": "proposed"
with a label, and a tool that filters by origin or label counted it as
a candidate.

Give the annotation a field of its own, PathEvent.kept ("startup",
"order?" or NULL).  JSON emits it as "kept"; label is left for
candidate identity, and real survivors are now "origin": "real".  The
text output is byte-identical: label and annotation are rendered
separately instead of relying on the leading spaces of the old label.
EXPLAIN (FORMAT ...) takes Kept from the new field, so the padding
strip goes away (and a candidate label is no longer shown as Kept).

The JSON format version goes to 1.2, since origin changes meaning for
these events; json-format.md lists the changes per version.

New pathprobe_kept slice: on the range + order query of pathprobe.sql
every annotated survivor is real and has no label, and the labelled
events of a proposed candidate are still proposed and carry no kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
